## psc/parse/state.pengu — estado, cursor, errores y construcción del AST.
##
## `PsParser` es el estado mutable de un parseo. Vive en la pila de la API
## pública; no hay estado global. El AST se transfiere al `PsParseResult` y las
## dos listas de trabajo (`child_stack`/`marks`) se liberan al terminar.
##
## ## Ganchos de módulos
## La gramática es mutuamente recursiva (`if` es statement y expresión, un
## bloque contiene statements, un statement contiene expresiones). Para poder
## repartir el parser en carpetas sin imports cíclicos, `PsHooks` guarda
## punteros a las funciones que cruzan esa frontera. La API los instala antes
## de parsear. Cada hook tiene un stub que no debería ejecutarse nunca; si se
## ejecuta, el parser falla de forma controlada.
##
## ## Memoria
## `PsParser` presta `SourceFile`, `LexResult` y `DiagnosticBag`. Es dueño del
## `PsAst` y de las dos listas de trabajo; `finish_parse` las libera.

import std.diagnostic as diag

import psc.span as pspan
import psc.source as psource
import psc.token as pstoken
import psc.lexer_state as psstate

import psc.ast.kind as pskind
import psc.ast.node as psast
import psc.parse.diagnostics as pdiag

insignia psc_parse_state_

## Opciones de parseo.
rune PsParseOptions derive Par, Nexus:
    ## Profundidad máxima de expresiones/tipos/bloques.
    max_depth as int
    ## Número máximo de diagnósticos antes de parar.
    max_errors as int
    ## Parar en el primer error (oráculos y `--stop-after-first`).
    stop_after_first as bool

## Opciones por defecto.
##
## ## Memoria
## Valor puro.
weave ps_default_parse_options into PsParseOptions:
    return with max_depth is 512, max_errors is 100, stop_after_first is false

## Ganchos que el parser de expresiones usa para entrar en statements,
## bloques y patrones.
##
## ## Memoria
## Los punteros a función no tienen heap propio.
rune PsHooks:
    ## `if`/`unless`/`while`/`for` en posición de valor.
    value as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int
    ## `when ... then ... else ...` o `when ...:` statement.
    when as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int
    ## `judge ...` y `judge ... over ...`.
    judge as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int
    ## `do:` como expresión de bloque.
    do_block as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int
    ## `with:` como expresión de bloque.
    with_init as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int
    ## `or:` de un `or_else_expr`; recibe el lado izquierdo ya parseado.
    or_block as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser, left as int into int
    ## Cuerpo de una cláusula `when ... -> ...`.
    when_body as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int
    ## Expresión completa (para átomos que contienen expresiones).
    expr as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int
    ## Expresión de lista, sin `and`/`or` booleanos.
    list_expr as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int
    ## Expresión de valor, admite `if`/`unless`/`while`/`for`.
    value_expr as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int
    ## Expresión de lista de valor.
    list_value_expr as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int
    ## Expresión sin cast (`expr_no_cast`).
    expr_no_cast as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int
    ## Guarda de `when` (`guard_expr`).
    guard_expr as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int

## Estado mutable de un parseo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Sin destructor. `ast` se transfiere al `PsParseResult`; `child_stack` y
## `marks` se liberan con `free_scratch`.
rune PsParser:
    ## Fuente; prestada.
    src as ref to psource.SourceFile
    ## Bag de diagnósticos; prestado.
    bag as ref to diag.DiagnosticBag
    ## Resultado léxico; prestado.
    lex as ref to LexResult
    ## Opciones.
    opts as PsParseOptions
    ## Índice del token actual.
    pos as int
    ## Profundidad actual.
    depth as int
    ## Profundidad de bloques.
    block_depth as int
    ## Número de errores emitidos.
    errors as int
    ## Modo pánico: no emitir cascadas hasta sincronizar.
    panic as bool
    ## Modo guarda: `->` no es acceso a campo dentro de una guarda de `when`.
    guard_mode as bool
    ## Parar el parseo (tope de errores o profundidad).
    stop as bool
    ## Último offset donde se emitió un error.
    last_error_pos as int
    ## Raíz del AST (`-1` hasta que se construye).
    root as int
    ## Arena del AST.
    ast as PsAst
    ## Pila de hijos en construcción (post-orden).
    child_stack as list of int
    ## Marcas de inicio de hijos por nodo.
    marks as list of int
    ## Ganchos a módulos.
    hooks as PsHooks

## Resultado de un parseo.
##
## ## Memoria
## `banish result` libera `ast`. El llamador conserva `SourceFile` y
## `LexResult` (el AST los referencia por índice).
rune PsParseResult derive Nexus:
    ## `true` si el parser no emitió ningún error.
    ok as bool
    ## Id del nodo raíz.
    root as int
    ## Arena del AST.
    ast as PsAst
    ## Errores emitidos.
    error_count as int

## Stubs de hooks. No deberían ejecutarse si la API instaló los reales.
weave _no_value_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "value"

weave _no_when_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "when"

weave _no_judge_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "judge"

weave _no_do_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "do_block"

weave _no_with_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "with_init"

weave _no_or_hook with p as ref to PsParser, left as int into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "or_block"

weave _no_body_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "when_body"

weave _no_expr_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "expr"

weave _no_list_expr_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "list_expr"

weave _no_value_expr_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "value_expr"

weave _no_list_value_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "list_value_expr"

weave _no_expr_no_cast_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "expr_no_cast"

weave _no_guard_hook with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return calling _hook_missing with p, "guard_expr"

## Emite un error interno de gancho y devuelve el nodo `error`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `error`.
weave _hook_missing with p as ref to PsParser, name as string into int:
    var off as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    calling ps_emit_issue with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseUnexpectedToken, off, off, "internal parser hook '{name}'"
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdError, off, off, 0

## Construye un parser vacío.
##
## ## Memoria
## Asigna las listas del AST y las dos de trabajo; liberar con
## `free_scratch` + transferir/liberar `ast`.
weave ps_parser_new with src as ref to psource.SourceFile, bag as ref to diag.DiagnosticBag, lex as ref to LexResult, opts as PsParseOptions into PsParser:
    var hooks as PsHooks is with value is (sigil of _no_value_hook), when is (sigil of _no_when_hook), judge is (sigil of _no_judge_hook), do_block is (sigil of _no_do_hook), with_init is (sigil of _no_with_hook), or_block is (sigil of _no_or_hook), when_body is (sigil of _no_body_hook), expr is (sigil of _no_expr_hook), list_expr is (sigil of _no_list_expr_hook), value_expr is (sigil of _no_value_expr_hook), list_value_expr is (sigil of _no_list_value_hook), expr_no_cast is (sigil of _no_expr_no_cast_hook), guard_expr is (sigil of _no_guard_hook)
    return with src is src, bag is bag, lex is lex, opts is opts, pos is 0, depth is 0, block_depth is 0, errors is 0, panic is false, guard_mode is false, stop is false, last_error_pos is -1, root is -1, ast is (calling psast.ps_ast_new), child_stack is list of int, marks is list of int, hooks is hooks

## Libera las listas de trabajo del parser.
##
## El AST **no** se libera aquí: se transfiere al `PsParseResult`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Libera `child_stack` y `marks`.
weave ps_free_scratch with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    banish p->child_stack
    banish p->marks

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cursor de tokens
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Número de tokens.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_token_count with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    return p->lex->tokens.len

## Corrige el helper anterior: devuelve un EOF sintético sin tocar el AST.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_current_token with p as ref to PsParser into Token:
    if p->pos < 0 or p->pos >= p->lex->tokens.len:
        return with kind is TokEof, kw is KwNotKeyword, start is 0, end is 0, line is 1, col is 1, aux is 0
    return p->lex->tokens at p->pos

## Token a `offset` desde el actual, o EOF.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_peek_at with p as ref to PsParser, offset as int into Token:
    var idx as int is p->pos + offset
    if idx < 0 or idx >= p->lex->tokens.len:
        return with kind is TokEof, kw is KwNotKeyword, start is 0, end is 0, line is 1, col is 1, aux is 0
    return p->lex->tokens at idx

## Tipo del token actual.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_kind_at with p as ref to PsParser into TokenKind:
    var t as Token is calling ps_current_token with p
    return t.kind

## Tipo del token a `offset`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_kind_ahead with p as ref to PsParser, offset as int into TokenKind:
    var t as Token is calling ps_peek_at with p, offset
    return t.kind

## Keyword del token actual (`KwNotKeyword` si no es keyword).
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_kw_at with p as ref to PsParser into KeywordKind:
    var t as Token is calling ps_current_token with p
    return t.kw

## Keyword a `offset` desde el actual (`KwNotKeyword` si no es keyword).
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_kw_at_offset with p as ref to PsParser, offset as int into KeywordKind:
    var t as Token is calling ps_peek_at with p, offset
    if t.kind == TokKeyword:
        return t.kw
    return KwNotKeyword

## Offset de inicio del token actual.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_current_start with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var t as Token is calling ps_current_token with p
    return t.start

## Offset de fin del token actual.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_current_end with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var t as Token is calling ps_current_token with p
    return t.end

## Offset de fin del último token consumido, o 0.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_previous_end with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    if p->pos <= 0:
        return 0
    var t as Token is p->lex->tokens at (p->pos - 1)
    return t.end

## `true` si el token actual es de tipo `k`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_check with p as ref to PsParser, k as TokenKind into bool:
    return (calling ps_kind_at with p) == k

## `true` si el token actual es el keyword `k`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_check_kw with p as ref to PsParser, k as KeywordKind into bool:
    var t as Token is calling ps_current_token with p
    return t.kind == TokKeyword and t.kw == k

## `true` si el token actual es el operador de `kind` con el lexema dado.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_check_lexeme with p as ref to PsParser, k as TokenKind, text as string into bool:
    var t as Token is calling ps_current_token with p
    if t.kind != k:
        return false
    var n as int is text length
    if t.end - t.start != n:
        return false
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of text
    var i as int is 0
    while i < n:
        if (calling ps_byte_at with p, t.start + i) != ((raw at i) to int):
            return false
        set i is i + 1
    return true

## Byte del fuente en `offset`, o `-1`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_byte_at with p as ref to PsParser, offset as int into int:
    return calling p->src.byte_at with offset

## `true` si el token actual es el identificador/soft keyword `word`.
##
## No asigna string: compara el rango del token con el literal.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(len), no asigna.
weave ps_check_word with p as ref to PsParser, word as string into bool:
    var t as Token is calling ps_current_token with p
    if t.kind != TokIdentifier:
        return false
    var n as int is word length
    if t.end - t.start != n:
        return false
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of word
    var i as int is 0
    while i < n:
        if (calling ps_byte_at with p, t.start + i) != ((raw at i) to int):
            return false
        set i is i + 1
    return true
## `true` si el token a `offset` es el identificador/soft keyword `word`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(len), no asigna.
weave ps_word_at with p as ref to PsParser, offset as int, word as string into bool:
    var t as Token is calling ps_peek_at with p, offset
    if t.kind != TokIdentifier:
        return false
    var n as int is word length
    if t.end - t.start != n:
        return false
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of word
    var i as int is 0
    while i < n:
        if (calling ps_byte_at with p, t.start + i) != ((raw at i) to int):
            return false
        set i is i + 1
    return true

## `true` si el token actual puede usarse como nombre de campo.
##
## Stage0 usa un lexer contextual: después de `.`/`->` un keyword duro puede
## ser un nombre de campo (`lex->antiquus`). PSC replica esa excepción solo en
## posiciones de acceso, no en declaraciones.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_check_name_like with p as ref to PsParser into bool:
    return calling ps_check_name_like_at with p, 0

## `true` si el token a `offset` puede usarse como nombre.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_check_name_like_at with p as ref to PsParser, offset as int into bool:
    var t as Token is calling ps_peek_at with p, offset
    if t.kind == TokIdentifier:
        return true
    if t.kind == TokKeyword:
        if t.kw == KwTypeOf or t.kw == KwSizeOf:
            return false
        return true
    return false

## Añade el token actual como nombre de campo, o emite un error.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_add_name_like with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    if calling ps_check_name_like with p:
        calling ps_add_token with p, p->pos
        var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
    else:
        calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseExpectedName, ""

## `true` si el token actual es el keyword `k` o el soft keyword `word`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(len), no asigna.
weave ps_check_kw_or_word with p as ref to PsParser, k as KeywordKind, word as string into bool:
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, k:
        return true
    return calling ps_check_word with p, word

## Avanza un token y devuelve el token consumido.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_advance with p as ref to PsParser into Token:
    var t as Token is calling ps_current_token with p
    if p->pos < p->lex->tokens.len:
        set p->pos is p->pos + 1
    return t

## Acepta el token actual si es de tipo `k`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_accept with p as ref to PsParser, k as TokenKind into bool:
    if calling ps_check with p, k:
        var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        return true
    return false

## Acepta el token actual si es el keyword `k`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_accept_kw with p as ref to PsParser, k as KeywordKind into bool:
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, k:
        var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        return true
    return false

## Acepta un soft keyword identificador.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(len), no asigna.
weave ps_accept_word with p as ref to PsParser, word as string into bool:
    if calling ps_check_word with p, word:
        var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        return true
    return false

## Consume el token actual o emite `ExpectedToken`.
##
## Devuelve el token consumido o el actual sin consumir si falla.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_expect with p as ref to PsParser, k as TokenKind, detail as string into Token:
    if calling ps_check with p, k:
        return calling ps_advance with p
    var off as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    calling ps_emit_issue with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseExpectedToken, off, off, detail
    return calling ps_current_token with p

## Consume el keyword actual o emite `ExpectedToken`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_expect_kw with p as ref to PsParser, k as KeywordKind, detail as string into Token:
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, k:
        return calling ps_advance with p
    var off as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    calling ps_emit_issue with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseExpectedToken, off, off, detail
    return calling ps_current_token with p

## Salta tokens `TokError` del lexer. Sus diagnósticos ya están en el bag.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1) por token saltado.
weave ps_skip_error_tokens with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    while (calling ps_kind_at with p) == TokError:
        var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p

## Salta `NEWLINE` (y `TokError`) sin consumir `INDENT`/`DEDENT`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1) por token saltado.
weave ps_skip_newlines with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    var more as bool is true
    while more:
        calling ps_skip_error_tokens with p
        if (calling ps_kind_at with p) == TokNewline:
            var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        else:
            set more is false

## `true` si el token actual es un starter de declaración/statement.
##
## Se usa para sincronizar sin saltarse el inicio del siguiente constructo.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_is_stmt_starter with p as ref to PsParser into bool:
    var t as Token is calling ps_current_token with p
    if t.kind == TokIdentifier:
        return false
    if t.kind != TokKeyword:
        return false
    var k as KeywordKind is t.kw
    return k == KwImport or k == KwInclude or k == KwLink or k == KwLdflag or k == KwInsignia or k == KwConst or k == KwVar or k == KwLet or k == KwStatic or k == KwSet or k == KwIf or k == KwUnless or k == KwWhile or k == KwFor or k == KwWhen or k == KwWith or k == KwDefer or k == KwErrdefer or k == KwBanish or k == KwReturn or k == KwBreak or k == KwContinue or k == KwRune or k == KwOmen or k == KwEcho or k == KwAlias or k == KwSeal or k == KwConcept or k == KwBind or k == KwWeave or k == KwEnchanting or k == KwDeclare or k == KwAntiquus or k == KwTest or (calling ps_check_word with p, "unsafe")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diagnósticos y recuperación
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Emite un issue y aplica el tope de errores.
##
## No duplica un error exactamente en el mismo offset.
##
## ## Memoria
## El `DiagnosticBag` es dueño del diagnóstico.
weave ps_emit_issue with p as ref to PsParser, issue as pdiag.ParseIssue, start as int, end as int, detail as string into void:
    if p->stop:
        return
    var off as int is start
    if off == p->last_error_pos and p->errors > 0:
        return
    set p->last_error_pos is off
    set p->errors is p->errors + 1
    calling pdiag.emit_parse_issue with p->bag, p->src, issue, start, end, detail
    if p->errors >= p->opts.max_errors:
        set p->stop is true
    if p->opts.stop_after_first:
        set p->stop is true

## Emite un error en el token actual.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_emit_here with p as ref to PsParser, issue as pdiag.ParseIssue, detail as string into void:
    var off as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    calling ps_emit_issue with p, issue, off, off, detail

## Entra en modo pánico y avanza hasta un separador.
##
## No consume `DEDENT` ni el starter del siguiente constructo.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(tokens saltados).
weave ps_synchronize with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    set p->panic is false
    var more as bool is true
    while more:
        if p->stop:
            return
        var k as TokenKind is calling ps_kind_at with p
        if k == TokNewline:
            var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
            return
        if k == TokDedent or k == TokEof:
            return
        if calling ps_is_stmt_starter with p:
            return
        var skipped as Token is calling ps_advance with p

## Exige fin de statement y sincroniza si falta.
##
## ## Memoria
## Puede consumir el `NEWLINE`.
weave ps_finish_statement with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    calling ps_skip_error_tokens with p
    if p->pos > 0:
        var prev as Token is p->lex->tokens at (p->pos - 1)
        if (prev.kind == TokDedent) or (prev.kind == TokNewline):
            return
    var k as TokenKind is calling ps_kind_at with p
    if k == TokNewline:
        var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        return
    if k == TokDedent or k == TokEof:
        return
    calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseExpectedNewline, ""
    set p->panic is true
    calling ps_synchronize with p

## Pre-scan de delimitadores antes de parsear.
##
## Replica B7: rechaza el token 513 de `(`/`[`/`{` con posición exacta. Los
## delimitadores dentro de strings/`antiquus` son un solo token, así que no
## cuentan.
##
## ## Retorno
## `false` si se superó el límite (ya emitió el diagnóstico).
##
## ## Memoria
## O(tokens), no asigna.
weave ps_pre_scan_depth with p as ref to PsParser into bool:
    var depth as int is 0
    var i as int is 0
    while i < p->lex->tokens.len:
        var t as Token is p->lex->tokens at i
        if (t.kind == TokLeftParen) or (t.kind == TokLeftBracket) or (t.kind == TokLeftBrace):
            set depth is depth + 1
            if depth > p->opts.max_depth:
                var detail as string is "{p->opts.max_depth}"
                defer banish detail
                calling ps_emit_issue with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseMaxDepth, t.start, t.end, detail
                set p->stop is true
                return false
        else if (t.kind == TokRightParen) or (t.kind == TokRightBracket) or (t.kind == TokRightBrace):
            if depth > 0:
                set depth is depth - 1
        set i is i + 1
    return true

## Entra en un bloque.
##
## ## Retorno
## `false` si se superó el límite (ya emitió el diagnóstico).
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_enter_block with p as ref to PsParser into bool:
    set p->block_depth is p->block_depth + 1
    if p->block_depth > p->opts.max_depth:
        var detail as string is "{p->opts.max_depth}"
        defer banish detail
        calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseMaxBlockDepth, detail
        set p->stop is true
        return false
    return true

## Sale de un bloque.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_leave_block with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    if p->block_depth > 0:
        set p->block_depth is p->block_depth - 1

## Entra en un nivel de profundidad.
##
## ## Retorno
## `false` si se superó el límite (ya emitió el diagnóstico).
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_enter_depth with p as ref to PsParser into bool:
    set p->depth is p->depth + 1
    if p->depth > p->opts.max_depth:
        var detail as string is "{p->opts.max_depth}"
        defer banish detail
        calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseMaxDepth, detail
        set p->stop is true
        return false
    return true

## Sale de un nivel de profundidad.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave ps_leave_depth with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    if p->depth > 0:
        set p->depth is p->depth - 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Construcción del AST (post-orden con pila de trabajo)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Empieza a acumular hijos para un nodo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Hace `push` en `marks`.
weave ps_begin_children with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    calling p->marks.push with p->child_stack.len

## Añade un nodo hijo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Hace `push` en `child_stack`.
weave ps_add_child with p as ref to PsParser, id as int into void:
    calling p->child_stack.push with (calling psast.ps_enc_node with id)

## Añade un token hijo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Hace `push` en `child_stack`.
weave ps_add_token with p as ref to PsParser, token_index as int into void:
    calling p->child_stack.push with (calling psast.ps_enc_token with token_index)

## Añade un hijo ausente (`None`).
##
## ## Memoria
## Hace `push` en `child_stack`.
weave ps_add_absent with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    calling p->child_stack.push with 0

## Cierra el nodo actual y lo añade al AST.
##
## Copia los hijos acumulados desde la última marca, los hace contiguos en
## `ast.children`, crea el `PsNode` y limpia la pila de trabajo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Hace `push` en `ast.nodes` y `ast.children`; no asigna por nodo.
weave ps_finish_node with p as ref to PsParser, kind as NodeKind, start as int, end as int, aux as int into int:
    var from as int is 0
    if p->marks.len > 0:
        set from is p->marks at (p->marks.len - 1)
        calling p->marks.pop
    var count as int is p->child_stack.len - from
    var first as int is p->ast.children.len
    var i as int is 0
    while i < count:
        calling p->ast.add_encoded_child with (p->child_stack at (from + i))
        set i is i + 1
    var id as int is calling p->ast.node_new with kind, start, end, first, count, aux
    var j as int is 0
    while j < count:
        calling p->child_stack.pop
        set j is j + 1
    return id

## Crea un nodo hoja con un token hijo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo y un hijo.
weave ps_leaf_token with p as ref to PsParser, kind as NodeKind, token_index as int, start as int, end as int into int:
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling ps_add_token with p, token_index
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, kind, start, end, 0

## Crea un nodo `error` de recuperación.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo sin hijos.
weave ps_error_node with p as ref to PsParser, start as int, end as int into int:
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdError, start, end, 0

## Convierte un `PsParser` en `PsParseResult`, liberando la pila de trabajo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Transfiere `ast`; libera `child_stack` y `marks`.
weave ps_into_result with p as ref to PsParser, ok as bool into PsParseResult:
    var root as int is p->root
    if root < 0:
        set root is calling ps_error_node with p, 0, (calling p->src.byte_len)
    var res as PsParseResult is with ok is ok, root is root, ast is p->ast, error_count is p->errors
    calling ps_free_scratch with p
    return res
